e files in your giant photo repository  that meet certain conditions in terms of  color scheme for instance the pricing  for making use of the vision API is a  dollar fifty per thousand units and you  get an initial allotment of units for  free the second API that we talked about  was the speech API the speech API  supports recognition of up to 80 plus  languages it can be real-time or  recorded so we showed you real time when  I was speaking into the web site and you  can build that functionality fairly  easily Google actually makes a quiet  library it's often optimised to detect  the active speaker even when there is  surrounding noise this is really  important because very often when  somebody speaking it's not in an  enclosed studio but rather they may be  out on the street  they may be in an open floorplan office  and you want to be able to extract the  speech from the primary speaker and  ignore the background noise and  background conversations if you are in  an environment where you have a lot of  technical jargon or words that would not  be common in everyday speech you can you  can actually provide word or phrase  hints to the API so you can say for  instance that gas and energy terminology  that isn't in everyday conversation  might be common in the audio inputs that  you're providing and so you provide a  list of those phrases and words and it's  more likely that they will be recognized  and like the vision API it can actually  identify inappropriate content and  filter that out pricing for the Google  Cloud speech API is six tenths of a cent  per 15 seconds with the first 60 minutes  being free the Google Cloud translation  API can work with a hundred different  languages as I noted in the example that  I gave in the customer success  application it can do automatic language  detection the model is being  consistently upgraded by Google so it's  constantly getting better you start with  a maximum quota in terms of the number  of characters that you can 